This is step 2, page 2. Look at the upper left area of ​​the screen. When starting a proof, first clearly indicate the assumptions, which are the starting conditions given in the problem, on the diagram. Here, the geometric starting conditions for constructing a square with the three sides a, b, and c (hypotenuse c) of a right triangle and each side as one side are depicted with blue symbols.

